{"reviewer":"senior-product-leader","findings":[{"title":"Parameterized template placeholders absent from rule resolver","severity":"P3","section":"Section 4","why_it_matters":"Origin §5.4 defines templates with parameterized generator calls, e.g. `Order-{number(1000,9999)}-{date}` → `Order-4821-2025-03-14`. The plan's U6 template resolver resolves only bare `{firstName}`-style placeholders against builtin generators and concatenates them; there is no parse step for `name(args)` and no test covers it. An implementer who passes every U6 test can still ship a template engine that emits `{number(1000,9999)}` literally, so any power-user rule written in the origin's own template dialect silently breaks — narrowing the Custom Rules differentiator KD3 keeps in scope. Fix: add a token parser plus a parameterized-placeholder test, or explicitly defer the syntax under Scope Boundaries.","finding_type":"omission","autofix_class":"manual","suggested_fix":"In U6, add a template token parser for `name(args)` calls (origin §5.4) and a test asserting `{number(1000,9999)}` resolves to an in-range value; otherwise list parameterized placeholders under Scope Boundaries as a v2 deferral.","confidence":50,"evidence":["Origin PLAN.md §5.4 example: `{number(1000,9999)}` and `Order-{number(1000,9999)}-{date}` → `Order-4821-2025-03-14` (generator invoked with arguments inside a template).","Plan U6 Approach describes template fill as 'resolve {placeholders} against generators' and the U6 test scenario asserts only `{firstName}.{lastName}@mail.com`; no `name(args)` token parser or parameterized-placeholder test is specified."]}],"residual_risks":["v1 Definition of Done is build-green + jsdom only; R10/R11/AE1 SPA event-sync and the headline 'works on React/Vue/Angular' promise are never validated in a real browser before DoD (manual browser smoke is deferred). For an external product, the deferred browser smoke — not the build-green DoD — should be the launch gate.","Readable-data quality is the product's core differentiator vs Fake Filler/lorem-ipsum, yet it is both scaled to a 'modest' hand-curated corpus (KD2) and unverified at runtime before DoD; the first real readability/variety signal arrives only in the deferred browser QA."],"deferred_questions":["Is the origin §5.4 parameterized template syntax (`{number(1000,9999)}`) a v1-supported capability or an explicit deferral? It is not addressed by U6's template resolver or tests.","For this external product, should a real-browser smoke gate be promoted into v1 Definition of Done, or is build-green + jsdom the intended 'implementation-ready' bar with browser QA explicitly post-DoD?"]}

